WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.560
A complete evaluation combines history, interview, direct

2
00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:07.180
assessment, analysis, report and results sharing.

3
00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:12.020
Hearing screening or recent audiological findings help address hearing as a contributor.

4
00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:16.000
The setting changes the immediate question: school evaluation examines

5
00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:20.820
educational impact; an outpatient evaluation considers functional outcomes;

6
00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:25.000
acute care may prioritize a targeted time-sensitive assessment.

7
00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:28.200
Open the interview with rapport, purpose and structure.

8
00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:31.000
Ask open-ended questions about the main concern,

9
00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:34.300
onset, change, consistency and everyday impact.

10
00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:39.840
Follow with specific examples and relevant developmental, medical, hearing and language history.

11
00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:42.920
Listen actively and clarify contradictions.

12
00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:46.020
A family’s priorities help shape the evaluation.

13
00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:50.720
A history is a starting point, and informant reports still need interpretation.

14
00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:53.640
Consider findings in the context of the history.

15
00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:58.460
A normal vocabulary score can coexist with difficulty conversing with peers.

16
00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:03.320
A low timed score can coexist with effective compensatory communication.

17
00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:06.060
Do not force a diagnosis from conflicting evidence.

18
00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:09.000
Further testing can accompany a diagnosis and plan.

19
00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:12.460
Recommendations specify goals, setting, frequency and session

20
00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:15.360
duration, based on the supported needs.

21
00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:20.060
A useful report includes identifying information, referral reason, history,

22
00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:24.740
procedures, results by domain, clinical impressions and recommendations.

23
00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:28.300
Explain quantitative findings and qualitative function.

24
00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:32.340
In the conference, use clear language, recognize strengths, allow

25
00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:36.260
time for questions, and close with next steps.

26
00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:39.700
Protect identifying health information when sharing records.

27
00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:44.022
A list of scores without functional interpretation is an unfinished clinical argument.
